# The refusal must name the OWNER and BOTH source constructor signatures as WRITTEN, plus the one CLR signature
# they collapse onto — a message that only said "duplicate .ctor" would not tell the author which to change.
# The written vectors are recovered from the pre-erasure carrier the declaration axis records for each slot, which
# is why they print with their `?` intact rather than as the `object` they collapsed to.
two constructors erase to one CLR signature
Bag
kotlin.collections.List<kotlin.Int?>
kotlin.collections.List<kotlin.Long?>
both become '.ctor(System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList<object>)'
